    dc:description "The image is a photomicrograph (PMG) of the lower epidermis of Aloe vera, viewed under brightfield illumination at 150X magnification. In an attempt to find alternative stains which are less toxic than conventional ones, Lamy fountain pen ink was used. Nuclei are stained blue, and the guard cells of a stomata are clearly visible (dark green/brown). The image was taken using an Olympus OIC student ";
